  "description": "Single slit for edge diffraction (UTD), the second scene of the diffraction set. A 3 cm one-sided square light (radiance 10000) at z = 0.5 faces two black jaws 5 cm apart. Each jaw is a closed 2 cm slab spanning y in [-1.5, 1.5] whose slit edge is a 30 degree wedge: a flat face at z = 0 towards the light and a bevel towards the wall, so the edge's exterior angle is 330 degrees (UTD n = 11/6) and the bevel stays in shadow. A white Lambertian wall at z = -1 receives the light. Geometric optics gives a fully lit 9 cm strip inside a 21 cm penumbra and darkness beyond; diffraction adds fringes and light inside the geometric shadow. At a design wavelength of 5 mm the Fresnel number is 1.5 and the light's transverse coherence width at the slit is 1.7 slit widths; scale all lengths with the wavelength. The camera stands between the jaws and the wall, facing the wall.",
